  "text": {
   "approach": "Same general Southern Pickets approach as the South Route — via Goodell Creek, The Barrier, and Crescent Creek Basin — continuing to the notch/saddle between Himmelhorn and West Twin Needle rather than climbing directly from the basin.",
   "approach_logistics": null,
   "road": "{\"name\":\"North Cascades Highway (SR 20) to Goodell Creek Road\",\"status\":\"Paved highway to a short NPS access road; open year-round at this low elevation (west of the seasonal Washington Pass closure)\",\"driveNote\":\"Trailhead is off SR 20 roughly 13 miles east of Marblemount and about 1 mile west of Newhalem (near milepost 119); follow signs from Newhalem toward Goodell Creek.\",\"seasonalGate\":null}",
   "overview": "The peak's original 1932 line: a moderate class 2 scramble up the west slope from the Himmelhorn-West Twin Needle notch, most often climbed today as one link in the multi-day Southern Picket enchainment/traverse; continuing off the summit onto the class 3 east arete toward East Twin Needle is part of the full traverse rather than a stand-alone descent.",
   "description": null,
   "descent": null
